C:Dr. William Boyce,1759
B:Joseph Barnes MS,Carlisle,1762.
R:
O:
A:England, Carlisle
N:Composed for 'Harlequin's Invasion' at the Garrick Theatre in 1759..
N:Two part arrangement - second part in bass clef..the standard words
N:are
N:included with this tune..Words of first verse written under stave..u
N:and d are in the ms.. At "symphony" "Sy" is written under the
N:stave..symphony = the West Gallery Music term for an instrumental
N:break..NB2 - could be a bar line here. Rest added by me to make bar
N:add up and match bass line. Z,X,Y,# as written.CGr
Z:vmp.C Graebe.
V:1 name=primo
V:2 clef=bass name=bass
